(5086051, 741899, 8860, '<td valign="top">This is obviously an accomplished shot but this kind of thing needs to be hangable to make it art, and currently the colour in this feels a bit drab and the viewpoint too high, so that the process looks too understandable (if that makes sense). A 90 degree plane with the water surface may yield more intrigue.<br/> <br/> Just a couple of additional points: 1. it''s over-sharpened, so I''d hold back a bit as it can spoil the subtleties, and it seems you''ve sharpened after adding a border. I''d do that last so you get a clean edge. 2. composition is a little awkward as it''s neither centred or thirds, etc..<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', 'This is obviously an accomplished shot but this kind of thing needs to be hangable to make it art, and currently the colour in this feels a bit drab and the viewpoint too high, so that the process looks too understandable (if that makes sense). A 90 degree plane with the water surface may yield more intrigue.  Just a couple of additional points: 1. it''s over-sharpened, so I''d hold back a bit as it can spoil the subtleties, and it seems you''ve sharpened after adding a border. I''d do that last so you get a clean edge. 2. composition is a little awkward as it''s neither centred or thirds, etc.. CheersJon', '2008-11-26 14:18:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5086054, 742128, 8860, '<td valign="top">Intriguing shot - a little too sharp but definitely memorable. Like the subdued colour, although that highlight feels just too obtrusive and it would have been more atmospheric to have a perfect exposure and fairly dim mood.</td>', 'Intriguing shot - a little too sharp but definitely memorable. Like the subdued colour, although that highlight feels just too obtrusive and it would have been more atmospheric to have a perfect exposure and fairly dim mood.', '2008-11-26 14:22:46.000000', NULL, 1),
